, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_9cf28e7b", "decision": "insufficient", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [767, 1635, 722, 302, 1719], "window": [20674, 59073], "confidence": 0.42, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "A static path 767->722->302->1635 exists, but 767's out-neighbours {722,988,1719} are disjoint from 1635's in-neighbours {106,133,302}, forcing a >=3-hop chain with two relay gaps each <=600 units. Both endpoints fire only ~7 times across 38k units (step_02), so the step_01 static connectivity runs through high-degree hubs and is not itself evidence of influence. Binned counts (steps 05/06) show joint activity only in two 4,800-unit bins - far coarser than the 600-unit relay budget - and 1635 is silent during 767's earliest activity. Without per-edge timestamps on the three hops the 600-unit ordering constraint can be neither verified nor refuted, so the evidence is insufficient rather than present or absent."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure (steps 01, 03, 04, 07, 08):** A static path does exist \u2014 767\u2192722\u2192302\u21921635 (722 reaches 302 per step_07, and 302 is an in-neighbour of 1635 per step_04). But critically, 767's out-set {722, 988, 1719} and 1635's in-set {106, 133, 302} are **disjoint**, so no 1- or 2-hop cascade is possible; any cascade requires at least 3 hops, meaning two intermediate gaps each \u2264600 units.\n\n**Volume control (step 02):** Both endpoints are very sparse \u2014 7 events each over a 38,399-unit span (~1 event per 5,500 units). So the static connectivity seen in step_01 is driven by hub intermediaries (81, 302, 62, 1814 are high-degree), not by dense endpoint activity. Static reachability here is weak evidence.\n\n**Timing (steps 05, 06):** Binned activity shows the endpoints are only jointly active in bins [30276,35076] and [49480,54280]. 1635 is entirely silent during 767's earliest activity (20674\u201330275). However, the bins are 4,800 units wide \u2014 nearly 8\u00d7 the 600-unit relay budget \u2014 so co-occupancy of a bin does not establish that the required hop-to-hop gaps are \u2264600.\n\n**Verdict:** I confirmed a time-ignoring path and ruled out short-hop (1\u20132 hop) cascades, but I have no per-edge timestamps for 767\u2192722, 722\u2192302, or 302\u21921635. The 600-unit constraint on a 3-hop chain can be neither confirmed nor refuted at the temporal resolution I obtained. Asserting \"present\" would rest only on static connectivity \u2014 exactly the insufficient signal the task warns against; asserting \"absent\" would over-read coarse bins.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_9cf28e7b\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [767, 1635, 722, 302, 1719],\n  \"window\": [20674, 59073],\n  \"confidence\": 0.42,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A static path 767->722->302->1635 exists, but 767's out-neighbours {722,988,1719} are disjoint from 1635's in-neighbours {106,133,302}, forcing a >=3-hop chain with two relay gaps each <=600 units. Both endpoints fire only ~7 times across 38k units (step_02), so the step_01 static connectivity runs through high-degree hubs and is not itself evidence of influence. Binned counts (steps 05/06) show joint activity only in two 4,800-unit bins - far coarser than the 600-unit relay budget - and 1635 is silent during 767's earliest activity. Without per-edge timestamps on the three hops the 600-unit ordering constraint can be neither verified nor refuted, so the evidence is insufficient rather than present or absent.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 24835, "total_output_tokens": 5751, "total_tokens": 30586, "total_latency_ms": 82664, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}